on the turn.\n\nReason:  \nI have no pair and only a backdoor flush draw. My hand is unlikely to be best now, and betting risks getting raised by stronger hands (A-x, K-x, sets). Checking maintains pot control and allows me to respond based on opponent action on the turn. It avoids turning my hand into a bluff unnecessarily while keeping implied odds if I hit a club (though only on both turn and river).\n\nAnswer: 0"}
