t first — likely strong.\n\nGiven you\'re in lead, minimize risk.\n\nReason:  \nMy hand is weak (king high, no pair, no draw), and opponent has shown strength by betting 100 on the flop. While the cost to call is small (100 chips, 0.5% of stack), continuing with no equity and poor implied odds is not justified, especially with the game nearing its end and my chip lead. Bluff-raising lacks sufficient justification given opponent’s likely range. Therefore, folding is the most prudent decision to preserve my lead.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
